From d82f169cb8bc1083ddf7c8565d13a9cc88ba2777 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VTSTech <veritas@vts-tech.org>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 05:57:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] Add on-screen stats overlay (FPS, backend, shader)

Draw a compact four-row overlay into the 320x200 software frame right
before presentation, on both the Vulkan and the classic SDL2 backend:
presenter (Vulkan | libslang-vk or SDL2 | classic), adapter / renderer
line, active preset with pass count, and smoothed fps + frame time +
feed mode. Rendered with the embedded public-domain font8x8 bitmap
font in palette-index space (I_GetPaletteIndex colors follow gamma and
pain tints), so on the Vulkan path the overlay goes through the shader
chain itself.

- src/i_overlay.c/h: new module (font table, EMA fps counter,
  palette-matched drawing, tail-clipping for long shader paths)
- i_video_vk.c: I_VK_DeviceName()/I_VK_PassCount() getters (from
  slangvk_device_info / slangvk_preset_pass_count; stubs when
  ENABLE_VK_SHADERS is off)
- Scroll Lock toggles at runtime (I_GetEvent); 'vkstats' config var
  (extra config, default on); -novkstats starts hidden
- README-VK: overlay section; fix the config file name/format (the
  fork's keys live in chocolate-doom.cfg, 'name value' form)

Validated on lavapipe under Xvfb (scripts/overlay_test.sh): 24/24
checks - default-on box, -novkstats and Scroll Lock each remove it on
both backends; overlay text decoded glyph-by-glyph from captured
frames on both paths; overlay fps agrees with -timedemo's summary.
